From 508ce8565c5946588e4c7bb722969a80bd96efa6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zirize <zirize@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 01:48:39 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 7/8] Read the screen off a real program, and say what a run
 and a state promise

Three of the gaps left were not bugs but blanks: things the suite had only
ever shown itself.

screen_text had never been read off a program that was printing. Bard's Tale
paints its own font into hi-res and never touches the text page, so every case
wrote the screen codes by hand, which proves the addressing and nothing else.
Applesoft is in ROM: boot, E000G, PRINT, and compare - the printed line has to
turn up, and every row has to match the harness's own decoder, which reads the
same cells by a different route. PR#3 hands the screen to the //e's 80-column
firmware, which is the first time the interleaved aux/main read has been shown
anything but bytes this file poked into those banks. Take the aux half of that
read out and the case fails.

run_frames' deterministic flag was tested while every tool in the workspace
but tas.py passes false, so what the path they use promises was never written
down. It is this: a frame is a frame only when the run was asked to be exact.
Turbo, and the full-speed path the core takes by itself whenever a drive is
spinning, both run a frame's cycles a hundred times over - three frames cost
51,093 cycles exact and 5,109,300 not. So a wait of sixty frames can pass six
thousand frames of game time and walk past the screen it was waiting for. Both
commands now say which they were, and run_until_change takes the flag instead
of being wired to false - defaulting the other way, because what a wait is
waiting for is usually a disk load.

And a save state rewinds the machine, not the disk in the drive. A game's
write goes through to the image on the host, so a load afterwards leaves the
file written while the machine goes back to believing what it saw before, and
nothing about the machine says otherwise. That destroyed a character disk in
this workspace once. Nothing here can fix it - a state carrying disk images is
a different feature - but state_save and state_load now list the drives the
rewind will not reach, so a client can refuse the combination, warn, or insert
the disk write-protected, which empties the list because then there is nothing
to disagree with.

50 cases.

